🔥MemoryLeak :
App keep reference of object that is no longer use [GC can not free their memory]

🔸MemoryLeakReason:
1- Holding Activity instance in singleton
2- Use Static variable
3- Using thread

Thread th = new Thread{
th.sleep(50000)
@runOnUiThread{
some ui component update
}
}
when user back press before thread is completed then it hold activity context cause temp memory leak

4-Using Handler

val handler = Handler(Runnable{
@run{
 some ui component update
}
},5000)
when user back press before 5000 then it hold activity context cause temp memory leak

5-Listener or callback not unregistered

6-Coroutine not cancelled
Using GlobalScope inside activity ,because GlobalScope lives independently of the Activity, the coroutine continues even after the Activity is gone.
Activity cannot be garbage collected until the coroutine completes.

🔸HowToResolve:
1- avoid using static variable
2- handle coroutine life cycle properly
3- clean up resource and callback
4- use leakCanary
5- memoryProfiler

🔸remember: P→C→C→D
Prevent — avoid unintended long-lived references.
Cancel — manage coroutine and lifecycle scope correctly.
Clean — unregister callbacks, listeners, and observers; clear bindings.
Detect — use LeakCanary, Android Studio Memory Profiler, and heap analysis.

🔥LeakCanary:Watch → Detect → Analyze → Report.
Leak canary is openSource automatic memory leak detection tool. which detect object that remain in memory than expected and analyse
heap dump and generate leak trace report..


         Activity.onDestroy()
                     │
                     ▼
          ObjectWatcher.watch()
                     │
                     ▼
            Wait a few seconds
                     │
                     ▼
          Trigger Garbage Collection [GC]
                     │
         ┌───────────┴───────────┐
         │                       │
   Object collected        Object still alive
         │                       │
         ▼                       ▼
      No leak              Heap Dump (.hprof)
                                    │
                                    ▼
                             analyzes heap
                                    │
                                    ▼
                           Find GC Root Path
                                    │
                                    ▼
                           Generate Leak Trace
                                    │
                                    ▼
                              Show Report


🔥Memory profiler: androidStudio-> profiler -> memory
Memory profiler is android studio tool help to detect memory usage in your app.
1-It detect memory leak by analyse memory usage in heap dump ..
2-It provide Retention size [total memory which will be free when object is garbage collected]
3-It provide swallow size [memory occupied by object it self]


🔥OOM
When App try yo allocate memory more than app available memory

🔸Reason for OOM
1-Large bitmap size
2-memory leak
3-Excessive memory caching

🔸How to avoid
1-leak canary
2-memory profiler to analyze heap size
3-DownSampling large Image bitmap
4-Limit cache size





